%0 Journal Article
%T Homomorphism Calculus for User-Defined Aggregations
%V 9
%U https://doi.org/10.1145/3763072
%R 10.1145/3763072
%X Data processing frameworks like Apache Spark and Flink provide built-in support for user-defined aggregation functions (UDAFs), enabling the integration of domain-specific logic. However, for these frameworks to support efficient UDAF execution, the function needs to satisfy a homomorphism property, which ensures that partial results from independent computations can be merged correctly Motivated by this problem, this paper introduces a novel homomorphism calculus that can both verify and refute whether a UDAF is a dataframe homomorphism. If so, our calculus also enables the construction of a corresponding merge operator which can be used for incremental computation and parallel execution. We have implemented an algorithm based on our proposed calculus and evaluate it on real-world UDAFs, demonstrating that our approach significantly outperforms two leading synthesizers.
%N OOPSLA2
%J Proc. ACM Program. Lang.
%I Association for Computing Machinery
%A Ziteng Wang
%A Ruijie Fang
%A Linus Zheng
%A Dixin Tang
%A Işıl Dillig
%D 2025
%P Article 294
%K Program Synthesis, User-defined Aggregate Functions, Homomorphism, Deductive Synthesis, Type-Directed Decomposition, Parallel Computing, Incremental Computation

