%T Domain-specific languages: an annotated bibliography
%V 35
%@ 0362-1340
%U https://doi.org/10.1145/352029.352035
%R 10.1145/352029.352035
%X We survey the literature available on the topic of domain-specific languages as used for the construction and maintenance of software systems. We list a selection of 75 key publications in the area, and provide a summary for each of the papers. Moreover, we discuss terminology, risks and benefits, example domain-specific languages, design methodologies, and implementation techniques.
